{
 "id": "hinge-leaf-petg",
 "brief": "One leaf of a small door hinge in PETG (FDM, printed flat, layers along Z). The pin is a 4 mm steel rod along Y through x = 0, z = 0; this leaf's knuckle is 30 mm long (y = 0 to 30), 9 mm outside diameter, and the pin turns in it. The leaf is a 4 mm plate (z = -2 to 2) from the knuckle out to x = 40, screwed to the door frame (the plane z = -2) by two M4 screws from the +Z side at (x 26, y 7) and (x 26, y 23). The door pulls on the pin 200 N straight away from the frame edge (-X), or 150 N off the frame (+Z), and hangs 100 N of its weight on the knuckle along the pin (-Y). Safety factor 3.",
